 ### [Learning Rate Scheduling](2701-learning-rate-scheduling.md)
-Learning rate scheduling adjusts the optimizer's step size during training to improve convergence stability and final reconstruction quality in radiance-field optimization [G]. It differs from static learning rates by dynamically scaling parameters based on training progress or structural changes, such as densification events [G]. This method builds on [Training Configuration](2332-training-configuration.md) by defining the temporal evolution of the learning rate parameter [G].
